scope: |
  THE OWNER CHOSE OPTION 3 of the DATASET decision in `v3/BACKLOG.md` (2026-08-10): `Dataset`
  written in ScalaScript as a library over lists, so BOTH v3 lanes get it with no host surface at
  all — the answer the project's own rule points at ("new intrinsics go to the plugin, never the
  core"). Options 1 (implement twice) and 2 (give `run-ir` a plugin path) are declined.

  That option was recorded as BLOCKED ON A PRELUDE, and the block is real: the corpus calls
  `Dataset.of` with NO import, v3's module system is markdown links, and `grep -rniE
  'prelude|auto-import' v3/src v3/ssc3` is empty. So this claim is two things, in order, and the
  second is worthless without the first.

  STAGE A — the prelude mechanism. A module loaded implicitly before the user's program, so its
  declarations are ambient. Reusing the existing loader rather than inventing a second path: the
  prelude is an ordinary module whose own markdown-link imports work as they already do. Must be
  overridable (`SSC3_PRELUDE`) so gates can run with it OFF — a gate that cannot turn the mechanism
  off cannot show what it changed.

  STAGE B — `Dataset` over lists. Counted from the corpus rather than guessed: `Dataset.of` 46
  uses, `fromTable` 11, `fromFile` 9, `fromList` 7, `fromGenerator` 3, `fromCsvAs` 2, and
  `run`/`runParallel`/`runShuffle` 1 each, with `collect`, `map`, `groupBy`, `reduce`, `sortBy`,
  `first`, `mkString` on top. The file- and table-backed sources need IO, which is the host surface
  option 3 exists to avoid — so those stay unsupported and the report will say so rather than the
  library pretending.

  The prize is capped and was counted by whoever filed the decision: N 166 -> 178 in their measure,
  12 conformance files, and only if each also passes the rest of its program. I will report what it
  actually moves, not what it could.
next: P-5 — measure the prelude's per-invocation parse+lower cost with the real library
